# App Storybook

- Export **one story** per file (e.g. `export const Main` or `export const Default`).
- Customize via **local interactive controls** (`useState`, sliders, toggles in the render), not multiple stories with Storybook `args`/`argTypes`.
- Co-locate: `Component.stories.tsx` next to the component.
- Group UI primitives under `"UI/ComponentName"`.

```tsx
export const Default = () => {
  const [value, setValue] = useState(0);
  return (
    <div>
      <MyComponent value={value} />
      <Slider value={value} onChange={setValue} />
    </div>
  );
};
```

Avoid spreading `args` across multiple story variants — prefer in-story controls instead.
